# An enum and a module folder may share a name (docs/module-model-options.md option B): the
# sibling `Color/` is the program's module folder `Color`, and `enum Color` is a type. A member
# after `Color.` that is an enum case is the case; one that is a function of the module is the
# call, as `Vec3.create` and `Vec3.vnorm` share `Vec3.` for lib/Vec3's type and module. (This case
# once tested a definition-site error for this pair, from when a folder of modules was a
# namespace of separate modules, and then the PascalCase-folder error of 0.3.174.)
enum Color { red, green, blue }

func main() {
  let c: Int = Color.green
  log("{c} {Color.shade()}")
}
